From b9719f1e182ef4ea5372d5c6870ffe5fe9fc9524 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nick Kennedy <nick@nick-kennedy.com>
Date: Thu, 22 Oct 2026 15:16:16 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] kosmickrisp: publish fdm_rate parameters in every
 non-resumed pass

Subsampled images received their rate map parameters once, by a GPU copy
recorded in the first pass that rendered them, after which a CPU-side
mark skipped further copies. When that command buffer was re-recorded
or dropped, as stitched chains that fall back are at startup, the copy
never ran and the image kept empty parameters, so later sampling used
the physical layout: Alyx's final eye image filled only the top-left
part of each view. The parameters are now copied in every pass that
renders the image and does not resume a stitched pass, sized to the
header and the map's parameter data.

AI-written commit text (biblioklept).

Generated-by: LLM
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
